waivers:
  - finding: "the test harness and the green-WU note fixtures restate xtask/tests/dod_gate.rs (a sixth private copy; tests/common/gitrepo.rs exists)"
    reason: "a real borrowing, left on purpose: rewiring six suites onto a shared builder is a change to the harnesses, not to the measurement, and this epic's WUs are read by the owner (plan, wu-review-evidence)"
  - finding: "record encoding is a hand-written key=value line format where the crate's other persisted records are serde structs"
    reason: "this file is a local reading a reader greps, not evidence that ships; the strict parser plus the terminator is what the tests pin"
  - finding: "LEVELS re-enumerates gate::Level::as_note_level"
    reason: "three strings used for parse validation and print order; deriving them needs as_note_level to become const, which nothing else asks for"
  - finding: "review_rounds counts any entry under refs/notes/cr, including one the gate would refuse to parse as cr/v2|cr/v3"
    reason: "a note on that ref records that a review run wrote there; reading each note body to mirror the gate's schema check would cost one notes-show per commit on the tip's line"
  - finding: "rounds are recorded when the gate runs, not recomputed at print time, so a tip re-gated after it landed (base == tip) records 0"
    reason: "the row shows the reading the gate took, and the aggregation keeps the largest one seen for that tip; re-deriving at print time would need the fork point the row does not hold"
  - finding: "date and base are written and parsed but never printed or asserted"
    reason: "the record is the artifact a reader opens beside the tip and the check ids; when a run happened and over what range is what makes a line readable"
  - finding: "a hook record carries no branch or unit identity, because the hook passes the resolved MERGE_HEAD sha"
    reason: "the hook has no branch name to hand over and a tip whose notes are absent has no identity to read; the level and the tip still name the run"
  - finding: "the cap's read-modify-write can drop a record appended by a concurrent gate run between its read and its write"
    reason: "appends are single writes; the truncation only runs past 2048 records, and a lost line there is a reading, not evidence"
  - finding: "every gate run pays three extra process spawns (~17ms, ~12% of a WU gate) and appends a line for a reading that may never be read"
    reason: "measured and accepted: this is the number W5 and W7 are adopted or dropped on, and the push sweep no longer multiplies it per commit"
